abstract: >-
  A deduplicated cross-disciplinary dataset of 2,000 unsolved, open and hard
  problems across 8 Macro-Pillars, 28 Superdomains, 8 Physical/Formal Substrates and
  7 Abstraction Layers (including 100 strictly non-duplicate open conjectures across
  all 25 fronts of Left to Solve, lefttosolve.com/programs), linked in a 6,108-edge
  knowledge graph that a Python (NetworkX) audit finds biconnected (0 articulation
  points, 0 bridges, 0 dangling links). It includes 103 audited Lean 4.35.0 theorems
  (of 117 declarations in lean/) without Mathlib about the atlas scoring software
  model (integer bounds of the scoring formulas, monotonicity of CSS, Titan and
  leverage, quadrant and era maps, taxonomy list sizes, a generic list-multigraph
  handshaking lemma, a dedup bound, the AutoResearch keep/discard rule, NonVacuity
  witnesses and AdversarialTests refutations), kernel-checked by Lean, with the 9
  Palomar comparator targets also accepted by six kernel checks across five distinct
  implementations; no Lean statement refers to the atlas data or its graph. Also
  included: an 11-page AMS-LaTeX white paper (15/15 title-verified citations),
  automated daily sync of 16 public open-problem trackers & 25 Left to Solve fronts,
  offline SQLite FTS5 hybrid search (100.0% MRR@5 on 25 benchmark queries), a
  13-tool stdio MCP server (incl. 59,396-target daily Left to Solve mirror & 290-problem crosswalk), 3 finite Track B probes (LOG-002, NT-005, COMB-002),
  a rubric sensitivity diff tool, 12/12 mutation testing, structurally verified
  DigiCert RFC 3161 and Bitcoin OTS v1 timestamps, and an AutoResearch evaluation
  harness (AQS = 98.35). Zero (0/2,000) problems are claimed solved.
